                    round1_title: 'Sales Order Rejection',
                    round1_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> A sales representative tries to create a sales order for customer C-4500 requesting 500 units of finished good FG-2000. The system rejects the order with error: <em>"Material FG-2000 not defined for sales organization 1000."</em><br><br>The material master record exists in the system and is visible in MM. Production has been manufacturing FG-2000 for months. The warehouse shows 800 units in stock.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Identify which module contains the error, the root cause category, and the correct fix.',
                    round1_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">SD: order rejected with an error ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">MM: material master exists, 800 in stock</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">PP: FG-2000 in production</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">FICO: nothing billed yet</span>",
                    round1_explanation: 'The material master lacked a Sales Org 1000 assignment in the SD view. Without this master data extension, SD cannot sell the material even though it physically exists. Fix: extend the material master to include the sales organization view.',
                    round2_title: 'Bill of Materials Defect',
                    round2_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> Quality control rejects an entire production batch of product FG-3000. The finished goods contain 3 kg of raw material RM-100 per unit instead of the required 5 kg. Production followed the system BOM exactly.<br><br>Investigation reveals the BOM was migrated from a legacy system 6 months ago and the quantity field was truncated during data conversion.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Identify the affected module, root cause, and corrective action.',
                    round2_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">SD: order confirmed</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">MM: 3 kg RM-100 issued per unit; consumption does not reconcile ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">PP: order run exactly to the system BOM</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">FICO: cost variance on FG-3000 ⚠</span>",
                    round2_explanation: 'The BOM master data in PP contained an incorrect component quantity from a flawed data migration. Fix: correct the BOM quantity for RM-100 from 3 kg to 5 kg and implement a master data validation process for all migrated records.',
                    round3_title: 'Phantom Inventory Crisis',
                    round3_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> Sales has promised delivery of 800 units to a key customer based on system-reported inventory of 1,000 units. When the warehouse attempts to pick the goods, they find only 200 units on the shelf.<br><br>The 800-unit discrepancy accumulated over several months. Goods receipts were posted in the system but physical goods were damaged and discarded without recording inventory adjustments.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Diagnose the module, root cause, and corrective action.',
                    round3_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">SD: 800 units promised to a key customer ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">MM: system 1,000 units, shelf 200 ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">PP: no change</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">FICO: stock valued at 1,000 units</span>",
                    round3_explanation: 'Warehouse staff discarded damaged goods without posting inventory adjustments in MM, creating a data quality gap between physical and system inventory. Fix: perform a physical inventory count, post correction entries, and implement mandatory goods movement postings for all warehouse disposals.',
                    round4_title: 'Lead Time Catastrophe',
                    round4_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> Production has halted on line 3. MRP generated purchase orders for critical component RM-500 with a 5-day lead time, but the actual supplier lead time is 15 days. Materials will arrive 10 days late, stopping production and delaying customer deliveries.<br><br>The material master shows a planned delivery time of 5 days. This value was set during initial system configuration two years ago and never updated when the company switched to an overseas supplier.<br><br><strong>Estimated damage:</strong> €200,000 in production downtime and late delivery penalties.',
                    round4_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">SD: customer orders waiting ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">MM: PO for RM-500 planned with 5 days</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">PP: line 3 stopped ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">FICO: penalties accruing</span>",
                    round4_explanation: 'The material master planned delivery time in MM was outdated (5 days vs. actual 15 days). MRP used this incorrect data to schedule procurement, resulting in late material arrivals. Fix: update the planned delivery time in the material master and implement periodic master data review for all sourcing-critical materials.',
                    round5_title: 'Invoice Price Dispute',
                    round5_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> Customer C-7200 has disputed an invoice. The sales order confirmed a unit price of €38, but the invoice shows €45 per unit. The customer is threatening to cancel a €2M annual contract.<br><br>Investigation shows the sales order was created with a customer-specific pricing condition (K004) at €38. However, the billing document picked up a different condition record (PR00 base price) at €45 because the customer-specific condition had expired between order creation and billing.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Diagnose and recommend the fix.',
                    round5_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">SD: order at €38, invoice at €45 ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">MM: no change</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">PP: no change</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">FICO: revenue posted at €45</span>",
                    round5_explanation: 'The SD pricing condition record (K004) had a validity period that expired before billing occurred. The system fell back to the base price (PR00). Fix: reconfigure the pricing procedure to flag condition expiry warnings, extend the customer-specific condition validity, and issue a credit memo for the difference.',
                    round6_title: 'Blocked Delivery',
                    round6_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> 2,000 units of product FG-1000 are packed and ready in the warehouse, but the system blocks the delivery. The block reason: "Credit limit exceeded for customer C-3100."<br><br>Customer C-3100 has a credit limit of €500,000. Their current receivables balance is €480,000 and this delivery is worth €75,000. The credit management configuration requires automatic blocking when the limit is exceeded, but no alert was sent to the credit team when the customer approached 90% of their limit.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Identify the issue and recommend a fix.',
                    round6_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">SD: delivery blocked on the dock ⚠</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">MM: goods picked</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">PP: no change</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">FICO: receivables €480,000 of a €500,000 limit</span>",
                    round6_explanation: 'The FICO credit management configuration lacked proactive alerting thresholds. While the credit block worked correctly, the absence of early warning notifications (at 80-90% utilization) meant no one could take preemptive action. Fix: reconfigure credit management to include automatic alerts at 80% and 90% thresholds, and establish a credit review workflow.',
                    round7_title: 'Production Cost Variance',
                    round7_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> Month-end closing reveals a massive production variance on product line FG-5000. Standard cost per unit is €12, but actual cost is €22 — an 83% overrun. Total variance for the month: €150,000.<br><br>Analysis shows the cost center allocation for overhead in the routing was set to cost center CC-4400 (administrative) instead of CC-2200 (production). The administrative overhead rate is €18/hour versus the production rate of €8/hour.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Identify the source and fix.',
                    round7_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">SD: revenue as planned</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">MM: material cost as planned</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">PP: routing overhead charged from CC-4400</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">FICO: variance of +€150,000 at month-end ⚠</span>",
                    round7_explanation: 'The production routing referenced the wrong cost center (CC-4400 administrative instead of CC-2200 production) in the FICO master data, causing overhead to be calculated at the wrong rate. Fix: update the cost center assignment in the routing master data and rerun the cost estimate for FG-5000. Implement cross-module master data validation for cost-relevant fields.',
                    round8_title: 'Vendor Payment Terms Error',
                    round8_desc: '<strong>Incident Report:</strong> The treasury department discovers a cash flow crisis. Over the past 3 months, the system has been paying vendor V-9000 on Net 10 terms instead of the agreed Net 60 terms. This vendor supplies €1.2M worth of materials monthly.<br><br>Investigation reveals the vendor master record was updated by a junior clerk who accidentally changed the payment terms from "Z060" (Net 60) to "Z010" (Net 10) while updating the bank details. No approval workflow was triggered for this change.<br><br><strong>Estimated cash flow impact:</strong> €350,000 in premature outflows over 3 months.',
                    round8_dataflow: "<span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">SD: no change</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">MM: vendor V-9000 record edited with the bank details</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-ok\">PP: no change</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-arrow\">→</span> <span class=\"erpcircuit-flow-symptom\">FICO: payments released on Net 10 terms ⚠</span>",
                    round8_explanation: 'The vendor master record in MM had payment terms changed without proper approval. The lack of a change management workflow for sensitive master data fields allowed an unauthorized modification to go undetected for months. Fix: correct the payment terms in the vendor master, implement dual-approval workflow for sensitive vendor master fields, and negotiate recovery of the cash flow impact with the vendor.',
